Thank you for using our software!
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A new installation of REST API module is a very straight forward process:

INSTALLATION
------------

Step 1. Uncompressing downloaded file.
-------------------------------------
   Make sure you have uHotelBooking script already installe don your website.
   Uncompress the REST API module version 1.x.x script archive.
   The archive will create a directory called "EXT_PHPUHB_MOD_RESTAPI".


Step 2. Uploading files.
-------------------------------------
   Upload content of this folder (all files and directories it includes) to following
   directory on your site:

   {your-website}/modules/additional/rest_api
   

Step 3. Running installation wizard.
-------------------------------------
   Log into admin panel of your sire as site owner or main admin and go to
   Modules > Modules Management page. Find on this page REST API module icon
   in Additional modules section. Click on [Install] link to perform installation.
   After successful installation you will see an appropriate message on the screen.
   Congratulations, you now have REST API module installed!


Step 4. Running tests.
-------------------------------------
	To start testing of these exampels do following:
	a. Generate API Key and API Secret in your account (you must be logged as admin or hotel owner)
	   on index.php?admin=my_account page
	b. Copy generated API Key and API Secret codes
	c. Open /modules/additional/rest_api/examples/include/config.inc.php file
	d. Enter copied on step #2 API Key and API Secret values in appropriate variables in your configuration file
	e. Enter your website base URL into $site_url in configuration file
	f. Run tests from following URL:
	{your-website}/modules/additional/rest_api/examples/examples-index.php


UNINSTALLATION
-------------------------------------
   To uninstall module go to Modules > Modules Management page.
   Find there there REST API icon and click on [Edit] link.
   In Edit mode find setting "Installed" and select "No" in dropdown box,
   then click Update button.
   After successful uninstalling you will see an appropriate message on the screen.
   

